<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Holland</h1><p class="st-meta">1806 CE – 1810 CE · capital Amsterdam</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Napoleon's client kingdom for his brother Louis, who tried to rule as a Dutch king and was removed for defending his subjects.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1806 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> replaced the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/batavian-republic">Batavian Republic</a> with a kingdom and installed his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-bonaparte">Louis Bonaparte</a> as king. Louis learned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a> the capital and turned its town hall into a royal palace.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Louis founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-netherlands-academy-of-arts-and-sciences">Royal Institute</a> and a national museum, introduced a civil code and took a sympathetic line toward <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> interests. He resisted conscription and enforced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-system">Continental System</a> only loosely, which allowed smuggling with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>. The economy suffered nonetheless, and the British landed on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walcheren">Walcheren</a> in 1809.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, angry at Louis's independence, forced him to abdicate in July 1810, and the kingdom was annexed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-empire">French Empire</a>. French rule ended in 1813, leading to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sovereign-principality-of-the-united-netherlands">Sovereign Principality of the United Netherlands</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-holland.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Holland" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Netherlands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1806 CE – 1810 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Amsterdam</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Louis Bonaparte</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Calvinism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Koninkrijk Holland</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1808&amp;focus=kingdom-of-holland" aria-label="Kingdom of Holland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4777 378 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Holland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5097 634L5097 634M5097 634L5054 728M5097 634L7959 2663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5097 634h0M5054 728h0M7959 2663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5097 634h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5097 634h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1808&amp;focus=kingdom-of-holland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
